WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.500
How might geometry be described by relationships?
A network is a picture of quantum-geometric structure.

00:04.500 --> 00:09.700
Tetrahedral shapes illustrate local building blocks.
The shapes make the local geometric structure visible.

00:09.700 --> 00:13.000
Now simplify the drawing to focus on the links.
A flat diagram makes the link relationships easier to follow.

00:13.000 --> 00:18.600
Binary signs live on links in the proposed effective picture.
An individual link can change its sign.

00:18.600 --> 00:21.766
A closed-loop product compares the full pattern.
See the interactive story for local convention changes.
